The process begins when an Incident requires further action. A Ticket is created and assigned to a Technician. The Technician investigates the reported problem and performs the necessary actions. If the problem cannot be resolved, the Ticket remains active and additional investigation is performed. If the problem is resolved, the Ticket status is updated and the Ticket is closed.
2.8.5. Maintenance Activity Diagram
The Maintenance Activity Diagram describes the workflow followed by a Technician when performing maintenance on an infrastructure device.
Figure 2.x. Maintenance Activity Diagram
chèn sơ đồ 
The maintenance process starts when a Technician receives a maintenance Ticket. The Technician reviews the reported problem, identifies the affected device, and performs an inspection. The required maintenance activity is then performed. After maintenance, the Technician checks whether the problem has been resolved. If the problem remains, additional maintenance actions are performed. Once the problem is resolved, the maintenance status and result are recorded and the process is completed.
2.8.6. AR Device Identification Activity Diagram
The AR Activity Diagram describes how the Mobile AR application assists a Technician in identifying a physical infrastructure device and viewing its information.
Figure 2.x. AR Device Identification Activity Diagram
chèn sơ đồ 
The AR process starts when the Technician opens the Mobile AR application and activates the camera. The Technician scans the physical environment to identify the target device. If the device cannot be identified, the scanning process is repeated. When the device is successfully identified, the system retrieves the corresponding device information, telemetry, and relevant Alerts. The information is then displayed through the AR interface, allowing the Technician to review the device condition directly in the physical environment.
2.8.7. Summary of Activity Diagrams
The Activity Diagrams describe the main operational workflows of AR-IMMS, from user authentication and infrastructure monitoring to Alert generation, Ticket processing, maintenance, and AR-based device identification. These workflows demonstrate how the different functional components of the proposed system interact during normal operation.
The diagrams also provide a foundation for the system design and implementation in the following chapters, particularly the Backend, Database, Collector, Web Dashboard, and Mobile AR components.
